            <ArticleTitle>A tortuous distal carotid artery: how to overcome the problem, with the aim of guaranteeing distal protection.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>77-80</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>This report describes a case of stent implantation in a right internal carotid artery with severe distal tortuosity, which caused difficulty in advancing a filter protection device. Advancement of the introducing sheath at the level of the carotid bifurcation and exchange for a third-generation distal filter protection device overcame the problem.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
